    "chapter_name": "Magnetic Effects of Current",
    "year": "2024",
    "shift": "shift_2"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two circular coils <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> turns each have same radius of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>π</mi><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The currents in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> respectively. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> are placed with their planes mutually perpendicular with their centers coincide. The resultant magnetic field induction at the center of the coils is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo> </mo><mi>mT</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo></math> ______. [Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "20",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Consider two coils as shown below:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0042_3b992698313f.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 170px;\"/></p><p>Magnetic field due to P, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math></p><p>Magnetic field due to Q, </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>net</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo></msqrt><mo> </mo><mi>mT</mi></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math></p>"
  }
}